Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-02
Subject: Pass ARM FindRegDeAlloc a base tai node
License: expat

`FindRegDeAlloc` walks the assembly list from `StartPai: Tai`.  The ARM
`MovLdr2Ldr` peephole only needs to start that walk at the list node after
`p`; that node can be a `tai_regalloc` marker rather than a `taicpu`
instruction.  Passing `p.Next` through `taicpu(...)` narrows before the
callee can inspect the node.  Pass the base `tai` node instead.

--- a/compiler/arm/aoptcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/arm/aoptcpu.pas
@@ -1269,7 +1269,7 @@
                         if taicpu(hp1).oper[1]^.ref^.index = taicpu(p).oper[0]^.reg then
                           taicpu(hp1).oper[1]^.ref^.index := taicpu(p).oper[1]^.reg;
 
-                        dealloc:=FindRegDeAlloc(taicpu(p).oper[1]^.reg, taicpu(p.Next));
+                        dealloc:=FindRegDeAlloc(taicpu(p).oper[1]^.reg, tai(p.Next));
                         if Assigned(dealloc) then
                           begin
                             asml.remove(dealloc);
